{
  "id": "sum-root-to-leaf-numbers",
  "questionId": "sum-root-to-leaf-numbers",
  "slug": "sum-root-to-leaf-numbers",
  "title": "Sum Root to Leaf Numbers",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Tree dfs",
  "patterns": [
    "tree",
    "dfs",
    "recursion"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "each path's number is built one digit at a time as you descend - what if the recursive call carried 'the number formed so far by the path down to this node'?",
    "at each node, the new running number is old_number * 10 + this node's digit",
    "when you reach a node with no children (a leaf), the running number IS the complete number for that path - add it to a total",
    "if a node has only one child, recurse only into that child; don't add anything to the total until you actually hit a true leaf"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "adding a partial number to the total at every node instead of only at leaves",
    "forgetting to check both 'index out of array bounds' and 'value equals -101' as the base case for a missing child",
    "starting the running number fresh at each node instead of threading it down from the parent (old_number * 10 + digit)"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Binary trees here are encoded as a flat array named `tree` using\ncomplete-binary-tree (heap) indexing:\n\n- the root sits at index 0\n- a node at index `i` has its left child at index `2*i+1` and right child at index `2*i+2`\n- a child index only counts as real if it's within bounds **and** doesn't hold the sentinel `-101`\n- `-101` means \"no node here\" and never appears as a real value, since every real node in this problem holds a single digit from 0 to 9\n\nEach path from the root down to a leaf spells out a number, formed by\nconcatenating the digits along the path in order, root digit first,\nmost significant.\n\n**Return the sum of the numbers formed by every root-to-leaf path in the tree.**\n\nA leaf is a node with no children. If the tree is empty, the sum is 0.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "0 <= number of real nodes <= 1000",
      "every real node value is a single digit, 0 to 9",
      "the sentinel value -101 marks a missing node and is never a real digit",
      "the total sum always fits in a standard 32-bit integer"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "an empty tree, represented as [-101]",
      "a single-node tree, whose one node is both root and leaf",
      "a root digit of 0, which still contributes its full leading position (e.g. 0->1 spells 01, treated as the number 1)",
      "a skewed tree with only one path from root to leaf"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "tree = [1, 2, 3]",
        "output": "25",
        "expectedOutput": "25",
        "explanation": "path 1->2 spells 12, path 1->3 spells 13; 12 + 13 = 25"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "tree = [4, 9, 0, 5, 1]",
        "output": "1026",
        "expectedOutput": "1026",
        "explanation": "path 4->9->5 spells 495, path 4->9->1 spells 491, path 4->0 spells 40; 495 + 491 + 40 = 1026"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "tree = [-101]",
        "output": "0",
        "expectedOutput": "0",
        "explanation": "an empty tree contributes no root-to-leaf paths at all"
      }
    ],
